+## What landed
+
+The `Status` column above is the per-idea record; this is what it adds up to.
+
+The single biggest lever was **#17's model swap**: `gemini-3.1-flash-image` became the pipeline
+default in the full-catalog regeneration written up in
+[`../docs/gemini-3.1-migration.md`](../docs/gemini-3.1-migration.md). That swap is also what
+superseded three ideas: **#1**'s re-inking and **#5**'s flat pupils simply went away under the new
+model, with no dedicated patch, and **#4**'s 4× night-sky spread was closed without its
+deterministic background-luma renormalizer — the whole catalog was regenerated against a tightened
+mood gate, `--night-luma-max 60` in place of the then-default 100 (60 has since become the code
+default, `NIGHT_BG_LUMA_MAX_DEFAULT` in `../lib/night-scores.mjs`), and shipped night backgrounds
+now span bgLuma 18–48 rather than 16–66. The two gate fixes the wave shipped alongside are **#11**
+(`../lib/solid-regions.mjs` whitens pen solid interiors out of the chalk keep reference) and **#12**
+(`judgeNightEyes` in `../lib/eye-fill.mjs`).
+
+The offline detectors and levers became pipeline code: the halo auditor (**#7**), the invented-shape
+detector (**#13**), the per-page notes registry (**#10**), and the two safety nets that gate CI —
+golden scores (**#23**) and the asset sha256 manifest (**#25**). Dark-mode chalk thumbnails
+(**#19**) and the proof sheet's `--source git:<ref>` comparison (**#21**) landed as generator
+features, and **#24**'s two orphan pages ship as `shapes/heart-*` and `objects/umbrella-*`.
+
+The eleven `NOT PROMOTED` ideas were not rejected — most are validated work that was simply never
+wired into the pipeline. The sibling-motif and coherence scorers still have no gate behind them
+(**#2**, **#3**, **#8**, **#9**, **#14**), as does **#18**'s deterministic painter. **#22**'s
+deliverable was a `gen:coloring-composite` CLI, which was never built — the composite render is
+still reachable only as the pre-existing `../lib/night-composite.mjs` its output was validated
+against. **#6**'s catalog-wide pen normalization + light regen also never ran: it used the
+already-shipped `gen:coloring-outlines:normalize`, and `../docs/gemini-3.1-migration.md` still lists
+that pass as the durable fix for the 39 remaining light-side flat-eye flags. Two ideas confirmed
+existing behavior instead of changing it (**#15**, **#20**), and one fell short in its own report
+(**#16**). Whatever from that set is still worth doing lives in GitHub issues labeled
+`area:asset-gen`.
 
